                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37b54a06-e546-3dfc-84e6-be7460a4192d",
                        "entry_id": "be2fab78-5ff1-36a8-9662-940c4460f6e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of supplying (oneself or others) with armor and (now especially) arms and ammunition in preparation for a conflict; the act of providing with the means of defense and attack."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "797ed60e-42af-4a46-966d-cfdd4dc31351",
                                "sense_id": "37b54a06-e546-3dfc-84e6-be7460a4192d",
                                "text": "The arming was now universal."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36cb8e10-5b65-4f53-98a5-0cd259f94d5b",
                                "sense_id": "37b54a06-e546-3dfc-84e6-be7460a4192d",
                                "text": "Applying the conventions of war epic, this section of the novel would correspond to the arming of the hero, his donning of armor and assembling weapons in preparation for battle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce39b010-da74-4a92-ab5c-16c52ee0ecef",
                                "sense_id": "37b54a06-e546-3dfc-84e6-be7460a4192d",
                                "text": "The arming of Paris begins [as follows...] First he placed along his legs the fair greaves linked with silver fastenings to hold the greaves at the ankles. Afterwards he girt on about his chest the corselet. […]The armings of Agamemnon, Patroclus, and Achilles with the same three lines as that of Paris."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4bedf5d9-1318-3851-ba96-12045d80a243",
                        "entry_id": "be2fab78-5ff1-36a8-9662-940c4460f6e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of supplying (oneself or others) with armor and (now especially) arms and ammunition in preparation for a conflict; the act of providing with the means of defense and attack.",
                            "The affixing and securing on of armor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially",
                            "in-compounds"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48634889-fffa-4432-a206-b4c29cfa0bcc",
                                "sense_id": "4bedf5d9-1318-3851-ba96-12045d80a243",
                                "text": "arming buckle, arming doublet, arming garments (garments for anchoring armor to), arming harness, arming jacket, arming nail, arming point, arming straps (for securing armor)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "28f0f20d-8b85-47fa-a434-9bda50505a41",
                                "sense_id": "4bedf5d9-1318-3851-ba96-12045d80a243",
                                "text": "[…] two tunicles and a gambeson, each with a border of the arms of France; […] a quantity of aiguilletes and laces for arming; six bascinets; a gamboised thigh-piece, and an esquivalens of leather[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bf9608f-0e34-3d66-861b-78e89eb68f84",
                        "entry_id": "be2fab78-5ff1-36a8-9662-940c4460f6e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of supplying with the equipment, knowledge, authority, or other tools needed for a particular task."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f8f800b-0e25-4254-904e-03d53742111d",
                                "sense_id": "6bf9608f-0e34-3d66-861b-78e89eb68f84",
                                "text": "The novelty largely consists in the arming of such subordinate officials of the statutory court with the new magic wand of the record book and of spoken English;[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d17288ae-2982-4e04-a61c-bb44575e009d",
                                "sense_id": "6bf9608f-0e34-3d66-861b-78e89eb68f84",
                                "text": "The Party has always seen to the selection of its most active fighters propagandists and lecturers , and to the arming of them with knowledge. The theoretical level of our propaganda depends primarily on them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a19c76da-b08d-484c-8ed7-e5e4e0c567ea",
                                "sense_id": "6bf9608f-0e34-3d66-861b-78e89eb68f84",
                                "text": "It may be even more confusing for a severely autistic child if they are not equipped with knowledge and skill […] It is the arming of a severely autistic child with information and opportunities to experience relationships […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe1cc069-32e4-3b0c-8991-8f0b325ecd4b",
                        "entry_id": "be2fab78-5ff1-36a8-9662-940c4460f6e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of preparing a tool or a weapon for action; activation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f32bc785-6615-47a5-a160-2232e257b6f2",
                                "sense_id": "fe1cc069-32e4-3b0c-8991-8f0b325ecd4b",
                                "text": "This insures the arming of the fuze when fired."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2abe0acd-bacb-41bc-8d1f-cff23eb291ec",
                                "sense_id": "fe1cc069-32e4-3b0c-8991-8f0b325ecd4b",
                                "text": "If he didn't knock it down, the second plane would have a shot prior to the arming of the missile's warhead. Suddenly things didn't look so bad. Blakely pushed the microphone button."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c660f03-1dae-3e37-b235-ca8a4ed87804",
                        "entry_id": "be2fab78-5ff1-36a8-9662-940c4460f6e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A piece of tallow or soap put in the cavity and over the bottom of a sounding lead to pick up samples of the bottom of the sea."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "06a3518f-c296-4e66-9654-78d9ff2859b5",
                                "sense_id": "9c660f03-1dae-3e37-b235-ca8a4ed87804",
                                "text": "the nature of the sea bed indicated by the arming in the cavity at the base[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
